SCOPE AND LIMITATION
--------------------
A copyright license governs copyrightable materials and the rights the
licensor actually owns. It does NOT give anyone exclusive rights in an
abstract idea, general scientific principle, method, or independently
implemented concept. It therefore cannot legally compel attribution from
all people merely inspired by the idea without using protected material.
No patent or trademark rights are granted or asserted here.

At founding, this repository consists of documentation, not executable
software. If source code is added later, its applicable software license
must be stated explicitly; Creative Commons does not recommend CC licenses
for software code.

This notice summarizes the licensing intent; the CC BY 4.0 legal code
